Below is the annual "official" /dev/null/nethack announcement.

There are to be a _lot_ of changes this year, largely having to do with
reducing the importance of the game score.  We also added a series of
"Recognition" trophies, which essentially rank a player's prowess with the
breadth of character possibilities.  This was put in largely to give Marvin and
Aardvark something new and challenging to aim for.  ;-)

Feel free to pass it 'round and submit it to any appropriate venues, should you
feel so inclined.

See y'all at midnight.

-robin

#####
The NetHack season is upon us once again.  Tonight (Halloween) at midnight
Pacific U.S. Time, /dev/null's Sixth Annual NetHack Tournament (<a
href="http://nethack.devnull.net">http://nethack.devnull.net</a>) opens. As
with past years, the Tournament is open to anyone who'd like to play. We're
also open to anyone who'd like to volunteer to run a game server since, though
we have four servers distributed around North America so far, play can be slow
across the transoceanic links.

/dev/null is a loose association of networking geeks, unincorporated and
noncommercial.  We just do this for giggles; we make no money from this other
than what folks feel like donating.

After last year's fiasco with eit_brad finishing the month with a score so high
it overflowed NetHack's internal score variable and ended up logged as a
negative number, we will be changing the trophy structure extensively this
year, primarily to de-emphasize the score and consider many other variables
which (hopefully) will reflect skill more than patience.

Due to this change, the scoreboard will not be completely functional at the
start of the Tournament and will probably be changed several times daily for
the first week or so.  ;-)

The prize structure going in (as we're always open to suggestions to change
this during the Tournament, especially this year), is:

Grand Prize Trophy:

	Best of 13
		the player with the most ascensions in 13 consecutive games, with no two
consecutive games having the same gender, alignment, race or role

Competition Trophies:

	Highest Score
		the player with the highest score which does not overflow the game's internal
score variable
	
	High Score (per Role)
		the 13 players with the highest score (which does not overflow the game's
internal score variable) for each character Role
				
	First Ascension
		the player with the first recorded ascension of the Tournament
		
	Fastest Ascension
		the ascended game using the lowest number of game turns
		
	Lowest Scored Ascension
		the ascended game with the lowest score
		
	Best Behaved Ascension
		the ascended game with the most successful conducts
		
	Most Ascensions
		the player with the highest total number of ascended games
		
	Most Unique Deaths
		the player who has died in the widest variety of ways

Recognition Trophies:
	
	These Trophies are to recognize significant displays of NetHack prowess.
	
		The Gold Star
			awarded to all players who ascend at least one game; the player will be said
to have "gotten The Gold Star"
		
		The Birdie
			awarded to all players who ascend at least one game from each gender; the
player will be said to have "shot The Birdie"
		
		The Double Top
			awarded to all players who ascend at least one game from each gender and
each alignment; the player will be said to have "thrown The Double Top"
		
		The Hat Trick
			awarded to all players who ascend at least one game from each gender, each
alignment and each race; the player will be said to have "done The Hat Trick"
		
		The Grand Slam
			awarded to all players who ascend at least one game from each gender, each
alignment, each race and each role; the player will be said to have "hit The
Grand Slam"
		
		The Full Monty
			awarded to all players who ascend at least one game from each gender, each
alignment, each race, each role and with each conduct intact; the player will
be said to have "gone The Full Monty"
	
	Additionally, any player who achieves one of these goals without completing
any games which were not necessary to meet the criteria for recognition will be
said to have done so "with bells on".  Thus, the highest achievement would be
to ascend at least one game from each gender, alignment, race, role, with each
conduct and with no games which did not meet a previously unmet criteria.  Such
a player would be said to have "gone The Full Monty with bells on".

Clan Trophies:

	Best of Show
		awarded to the Clan with the highest collective Tournament score as
calculated by adding the point values below:
			Best of 13 = 5
			Highest Score = 3
			High Score (Role) = 1
			First Ascension = 3
			Fastest Ascension = 4
			Lowest Scored Ascension = 4
			Best Behaved Ascension = 4
			Most Ascensions = 4
			Most Unique Deaths = 4
			The Gold Star = 1
			The Birdie = 2
			The Double Top = 3
			The Hat Trick = 4
			The Grand Slam = 5
			The Full Monty = 10

Server Requirements:

This year's Tournament will begin with servers in California, Oklahoma, Oregon
and Finland, but with additional servers hopefully coming online in the first
few days.  Since we always appreciate additional volunteer servers to help
speed the game play up for folks not near an existing host, here's roughly what
you need to volunteer a game server (Remember, before volunteering, that anyone
with admin level access to a game server box is not allowed to compete; so
don't volunteer to host if you want to be a contender):

	a multi-user 3.4.3 NetHack installation (thus, probably, a Unix of some sort;
the /dev/null server is an OpenBSD system)
	an installed copy of our game server kit (<a
href="http://nethack.devnull.net/software">http://nethack.devnull.net/software</
a>)
	sufficient speed/disk/memory to support 2500 player accounts and 26 concurrent
players (ours is a P133 with 32M of memory and 5G of disk)
	a dedicated Internet connection (ours is on a T1; cable modems and DSL will
work fine, but it's dificult to do unless you have static IP numbers)
	since NetHack needs real user accounts, we'd recommend that it be a dedicated
system (the players will need to be entered in /etc/passwd to play on the box)
